p.src:
Why does Eq. [eq:l4-proper-time] equal a clock reading? For a clock at rest, $\Delta x=0$, so $\Delta\tau=\Delta t$. For a uniformly moving clock, choose the primed frame in which that clock is at rest. There $\Delta x'=0$, and invariance gives $\Delta\tau
=\sqrt{\Delta t'^2-\Delta x'^2}
=\Delta t'.$ Moving clocks therefore tick off proper time.

